# =============================================================================
# Request wire corpus — the /generate body contract, row by row
# =============================================================================
#
# 124 request bodies and the outcome the request parser records for each, in the
# shape `ok|prompt=...|field=value` or `err|<400 body error>`. The corpus was
# first run through the retired hand-written parser (JsonCursor, json_parse_*);
# 83 rows came out the same through `norma:json`, and the other 41 differ only
# where the minimal parser was not JSON:
#
#   - Wording of syntax errors. Norma names the offence and its position
#     (`trailing characters at position 16`), where the retired parser said
#     `trailing content after object`. The status (400) and the `malformed JSON:`
#     prefix are the same. 29 rows.
#   - Accepted before, refused now: a leading zero (`01`), and an unescaped
#     control character (newline, tab, U+0001) inside a string. 4 rows.
#   - Refused before, accepted now: `\uXXXX` escapes, in values and in keys, which
#     the minimal parser refused as "not supported". 4 rows.
#   - Which error wins when a body has two. The retired parser checked fields as
#     it read them; Norma parses the whole body first, so a syntax error anywhere
#     wins over a schema error, and schema errors are checked in field-name order.
#     4 rows.
#
# Everything else is identical: the schema errors (unknown, duplicate, wrong
# type, empty or missing prompt), the integer range bound, number conversion,
# and the order and values of every accepted field.

